-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- THE PENSIONABLE EARNINGS OF A MONTH (sections 51 to 51.3).
--
-- Section 51(1) gives the pensionable earnings, first additional pensionable earnings and second
-- additional pensionable earnings of a contributor for one month as a product A x B. A is the
-- earnings for which section 52, 52.1 or 52.2 deems a contribution made for the month (the
-- modules cp3-deemed-contributions.l4) or, for a disabled contributor's additional earnings, the
-- greatest of three amounts, one of which comes from the formula of section 51.1 or 51.2. B is a ratio
-- that brings the month's earnings up to the level of the year in which a benefit becomes payable.
--
-- The figures that other sections give (the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average, the Pension Index,
-- the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings) are plain inputs here, with the section named.

§ `Part II -- Division B -- pensionable earnings of a month (sections 51 to 51.3)`

§§ `51(1) -- B, the ratio that carries a month's earnings forward`

-- src:1187 | B is
-- src:1188 | (a) where the contributor was born after December 31, 1932 and the contributor’s retirement pension did not commence before January 1, 1998 and, after the contributor’s 60th birthday, a month was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period by reason of disability, the product determined by the formula
-- src:1189 | (C/D) × (E/F)
-- src:1190 | where
-- src:1191 | C is the contributor’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit first became payable to the contributor under this Act or a provincial pension plan that caused a month after the contributor’s 60th birthday to be excluded from the contributor’s contributory period by reason of disability,
-- src:1192 | D is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month,
-- src:1193 | E is the Pension Index for the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor under this Act or a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:1194 | F is the Pension Index for the year referred to in the description of C, and
-- src:1195 | (b) in any other case, the ratio
-- src:1196 | G/D
-- src:1197 | where
-- src:1198 | G is the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average in respect of the contributor for the year in which a benefit becomes payable to the contributor under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:1199 | D is as described in paragraph (a).
@ref Act s 51(1) description of B (src:1187-1199)
GIVEN events IS A `cp3 Life events of a contributor`
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit first became payable that caused a month after the 60th birthday to be excluded by reason of disability (C)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (E)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Pension Index for the year referred to in the description of C (F)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (G)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for a contributor born after 1932, whose retirement pension did not start before 1998
-- and who had a month excluded for disability after the 60th birthday, B is (C / D) x (E / F);
-- for everyone else B is G / D. The 60th birthday is the actual birthday (the text says "birthday"
-- and not "reaches"), and "after" it is read as a month later than the month that contains it.
-- NOTHING means a figure the ratio divides by is zero.
-- out of range: section 18 (piece cp1): the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings are taken as numbers.
`s 51(1) — B, the ratio applied to a month's earnings` events `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit first became payable that caused a month after the 60th birthday to be excluded by reason of disability (C)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)` `the Pension Index for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (E)` `the Pension Index for the year referred to in the description of C (F)` `the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (G)` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a) of B applies`
    THEN (IF `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)` EQUALS 0 OR `the Pension Index for the year referred to in the description of C (F)` EQUALS 0
          THEN NOTHING
          ELSE JUST ((`the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit first became payable that caused a month after the 60th birthday to be excluded by reason of disability (C)` DIVIDED BY `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)`)
                     TIMES (`the Pension Index for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (E)` DIVIDED BY `the Pension Index for the year referred to in the description of C (F)`)))
    ELSE (IF `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)` EQUALS 0
          THEN NOTHING
          ELSE JUST (`the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year in which a benefit becomes payable under this Act or a provincial pension plan (G)` DIVIDED BY `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month (D)`))
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) of B applies` MEANS
                `the contributor was born after December 31, 1932`
            AND `the contributor's retirement pension did not commence before January 1, 1998`
            AND `after the contributor's 60th birthday a month was excluded by reason of disability`
        `the contributor was born after December 31, 1932` MEANS
            events's `the contributor's date of birth` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1933 1 1)
        `the contributor's retirement pension did not commence before January 1, 1998` MEANS
            CONSIDER events's `the month with which a retirement pension becomes payable, if it does`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST started THEN started AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1)
        `after the contributor's 60th birthday a month was excluded by reason of disability` MEANS
            any (GIVEN m YIELD `the month of a date` m AT LEAST `the month after the 60th birthday`) `the months excluded by reason of disability`
        `the month after the 60th birthday` MEANS
            `the month following the month of a date` (`the date a person actually reaches a specified age` (events's `the contributor's date of birth`) 60)
        `the months excluded by reason of disability` MEANS
            events's `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability`

§§ `51(1) -- the pensionable earnings of a month, tier by tier`

-- src:1174 | 51 (1) The pensionable earnings, first additional pensionable earnings or second additional pensionable earnings, as the case may be, of a contributor for a month (in this subsection referred to as the “particular month”) are an amount determined by the formula
-- src:1175 | A × B
-- src:1176 | where
-- src:1177 | A is
-- src:1178 | (a) in the case of pensionable earnings, earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52 to have made a base contribution for the particular month;
@ref Act s 51(1), (1)(a) (src:1174-1178)
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER
      B IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the pensionable earnings of a month are A x B, where A is the earnings for which
-- section 52 deems a base contribution made for the month.
`s 51(1)(a) — the pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month` `A` B MEANS
    CONSIDER B
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (`A` TIMES b)

-- src:1179 | (b) in the case of first additional pensionable earnings, earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.1 to have made a first additional contribution for the particular month, except in the case where the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month, for the calculation of a pension or benefit other than a disability pension, the greatest of the following amounts:
-- src:1180 | (i) the value determined in accordance with section 51.1 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12,
-- src:1181 | (ii) the highest of any value determined in accordance with section 51.1 for any of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled, multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12, and
-- src:1182 | (iii) the earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.1 to have made a first additional contribution for the particular month; or
@ref Act s 51(1)(b) (src:1179-1182)
GIVEN `the earnings for which section 52.1 deems a first additional contribution made for the particular month` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value determined in accordance with section 51.1 for the particular month` IS A NUMBER
      `the values determined in accordance with section 51.1 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: A for first additional pensionable earnings is the earnings section 52.1 deems, except
-- that for a contributor who is disabled in the month, when the pension or benefit is not a disability
-- pension, it is the greatest of (i) the section 51.1 value of the month, (ii) the highest section 51.1
-- value of the 72 months before the month of deemed disablement (each times the Year's Maximum
-- Pensionable Earnings, divided by 12) and (iii) the section 52.1 earnings.
`s 51(1)(b) — A, the first additional earnings for a month` `the earnings for which section 52.1 deems a first additional contribution made for the particular month` `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension` `the value determined in accordance with section 51.1 for the particular month` `the values determined in accordance with section 51.1 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month` MEANS
    IF `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` AND `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension`
    THEN max (max `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`) `the earnings for which section 52.1 deems a first additional contribution made for the particular month`
    ELSE `the earnings for which section 52.1 deems a first additional contribution made for the particular month`
    WHERE
        `limb (i)` MEANS (`the value determined in accordance with section 51.1 for the particular month` TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
            IF null `the values determined in accordance with section 51.1 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled`
            THEN 0
            ELSE (maximum `the values determined in accordance with section 51.1 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- src:1183 | (c) in the case of second additional pensionable earnings, earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.2 to have made a second additional contribution for the particular month except in the case where the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month, for the calculation of a pension or benefit other than a disability pension, the greatest of the following amounts:
-- src:1184 | (i) the value determined in accordance with section 51.2 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12,
-- src:1185 | (ii) the highest of any value determined in accordance with section 51.2 for any of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled, multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12, and
-- src:1186 | (iii) the earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.2 to have made a second additional contribution for the particular month; and
@ref Act s 51(1)(c) (src:1183-1186)
GIVEN `the earnings for which section 52.2 deems a second additional contribution made for the particular month` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value determined in accordance with section 51.2 for the particular month` IS A NUMBER
      `the values determined in accordance with section 51.2 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the same as paragraph (b), with the second additional contribution and section 51.2.
`s 51(1)(c) — A, the second additional earnings for a month` `the earnings for which section 52.2 deems a second additional contribution made for the particular month` `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension` `the value determined in accordance with section 51.2 for the particular month` `the values determined in accordance with section 51.2 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month` MEANS
    IF `the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month` AND `the calculation is for a pension or benefit other than a disability pension`
    THEN max (max `limb (i)` `limb (ii)`) `the earnings for which section 52.2 deems a second additional contribution made for the particular month`
    ELSE `the earnings for which section 52.2 deems a second additional contribution made for the particular month`
    WHERE
        `limb (i)` MEANS (`the value determined in accordance with section 51.2 for the particular month` TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month`) DIVIDED BY 12
        `limb (ii)` MEANS
            IF null `the values determined in accordance with section 51.2 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled`
            THEN 0
            ELSE (maximum `the values determined in accordance with section 51.2 for each of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled` TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month`) DIVIDED BY 12

-- src:1201 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), the first additional pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month are an amount calculated as provided in subsection (1) multiplied
-- src:1202 | (a) for 2019, by 0.15;
-- src:1203 | (b) for 2020, by 0.3;
-- src:1204 | (c) for 2021, by 0.5; and
-- src:1205 | (d) for 2022, by 0.75.
@ref Act s 51(1.1) (src:1201-1205)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the first additional pensionable earnings of a month in 2019, 2020, 2021 and 2022 are
-- the amount under subsection (1) multiplied by 0.15, 0.3, 0.5 and 0.75. NOTHING means the year is
-- not one of those four, and the subsection multiplies nothing.
`s 51(1.1) — the multiplier of the first additional pensionable earnings of a month in a year` year MEANS
    BRANCH IF year EQUALS 2019 THEN JUST 0.15
           IF year EQUALS 2020 THEN JUST 0.3
           IF year EQUALS 2021 THEN JUST 0.5
           IF year EQUALS 2022 THEN JUST 0.75
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1175 | A × B
-- src:1176 | where
-- src:1177 | A is
-- src:1179 | (b) in the case of first additional pensionable earnings, earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.1 to have made a first additional contribution for the particular month, except in the case where the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month, for the calculation of a pension or benefit other than a disability pension, the greatest of the following amounts:
-- src:1180 | (i) the value determined in accordance with section 51.1 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12,
-- src:1181 | (ii) the highest of any value determined in accordance with section 51.1 for any of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled, multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12, and
-- src:1182 | (iii) the earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.1 to have made a first additional contribution for the particular month; or
-- src:1201 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), the first additional pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month are an amount calculated as provided in subsection (1) multiplied
-- src:1202 | (a) for 2019, by 0.15;
-- src:1203 | (b) for 2020, by 0.3;
-- src:1204 | (c) for 2021, by 0.5; and
-- src:1205 | (d) for 2022, by 0.75.
@ref Act s 51(1)(b), (1.1) (src:1175-1205)
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER
      B IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the first additional pensionable earnings of a month are A x B, multiplied for the
-- months of 2019 to 2022 by the multiplier of subsection (1.1) ("despite subsection (1)").
`s 51(1)(b) — the first additional pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month` `A` B year MEANS
    CONSIDER B
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (`A` TIMES b TIMES (fromMaybe 1 (`s 51(1.1) — the multiplier of the first additional pensionable earnings of a month in a year` year)))

-- src:1183 | (c) in the case of second additional pensionable earnings, earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.2 to have made a second additional contribution for the particular month except in the case where the contributor is considered to be disabled for the purposes of this Act or a provincial pension plan during the particular month, for the calculation of a pension or benefit other than a disability pension, the greatest of the following amounts:
-- src:1184 | (i) the value determined in accordance with section 51.2 multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12,
-- src:1185 | (ii) the highest of any value determined in accordance with section 51.2 for any of the 72 months before the month in which the contributor was deemed to have become disabled, multiplied by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year that includes the particular month, divided by 12, and
-- src:1186 | (iii) the earnings for which the contributor is deemed by section 52.2 to have made a second additional contribution for the particular month; and
@ref Act s 51(1)(c) (src:1183-1186)
GIVEN `A` IS A NUMBER
      B IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 51(1)(c) — the second additional pensionable earnings of a contributor for a month` `A` B MEANS
    CONSIDER B
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (`A` TIMES b)

§§ `51(2) and 51(3) -- the figures behind C, for years long past`

-- src:1207 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), in the case of pensionable earnings, if the year referred to in the description of C is 1987 or earlier, the Maximum Pensionable Earnings Average for the year is calculated as if the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for a particular year before 1986 were calculated as the greatest multiple of $100 that is equal to or less than an amount calculated by multiplying the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for 1986, which are $25,800, by the ratio
-- src:1208 | A/B
-- src:1209 | where
-- src:1210 | A is the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year preceding that particular year of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada as published by Statistics Canada for each month in that period, and
-- src:1211 | B is the average for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1985 of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada as published by Statistics Canada for each month in that period.
@ref Act s 51(2) (src:1207-1211)
GIVEN `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year preceding the particular year (A)` IS A NUMBER
      `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1985 (B)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: when the year of C is 1987 or earlier, the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year
-- before 1986 is taken to be the greatest multiple of $100 not more than $25,800 (the figure for 1986)
-- times A / B. The Statistics Canada averages are plain inputs. NOTHING means B is zero.
-- out of range: the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada, as published by Statistics Canada (not among the inputs): taken as numbers.
`s 51(2) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings taken for a year before 1986` `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year preceding the particular year (A)` `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1985 (B)` MEANS
    IF `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1985 (B)` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((FLOOR ((25800 TIMES `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year preceding the particular year (A)`
                         DIVIDED BY `the average of the average weekly wages and salaries of the Industrial Composite in Canada for the twelve month period ending on June 30, 1985 (B)`) DIVIDED BY 100)) TIMES 100)

-- src:1213 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), in the case of pensionable earnings, if the beginning of a period that is excluded from the contributor’s contributory period by reason of disability is in a year before 1974, in calculating the Pension Index for the year in which that period begins, paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan, R.S.C. 1970, c. C-5, as amended by section 24 of chapter 4 of the Statutes of Canada, 1974-75-76, is to be read without reference to the words “or 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year, whichever is the lesser”.
@ref Act s 51(3) (src:1213)
GIVEN `the year in which the period excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability begins` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- Plain gloss: for pensionable earnings, when the excluded period begins in a year before 1974, the
-- Pension Index of that year is worked out as if paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan,
-- R.S.C. 1970, c. C-5, did not have the words "or 1.02 times the Pension Index for the preceding year,
-- whichever is the lesser". JUST FALSE means the words are not read in; NOTHING means the subsection
-- says nothing about the year (the 1970 Act is not among the texts this piece reads).
-- out of range: paragraph 43.1(2)(a) of the Canada Pension Plan, R.S.C. 1970, c. C-5 (another Act, not among the inputs).
`s 51(3) — the words about 1.02 times the preceding year's Pension Index are read into the 1970 Act's calculation` `the year in which the period excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability begins` MEANS
    IF `the year in which the period excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability begins` LESS THAN 1974
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `51.1 and 51.2 -- the value determined for each month excluded by reason of disability`

-- Not a provision: sections 51.1(1) and 51.2(1) give the same formula for the first and the second
-- additional contributory period, so the arithmetic is written once and each section calls it.
-- Each of A to F is the greater of a ratio and any value already determined for a month of that year;
-- G is the same for the year of deemed disablement, with the ratio capped at 1.
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the greatest of the values already determined for a month of a year` year MEANS
    IF null (year's `values already determined for a month of that year`) THEN 0 ELSE maximum (year's `values already determined for a month of that year`)

-- Not a provision: the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year of the lookback, prorated by the
-- months of the additional contributory period when that period begins in the year (sections 51.1(2) and
-- 51.2(2): A x (M / 12)).
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year of the lookback, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year MEANS
    IF year's `the additional contributory period begins in that year`
    THEN (year's `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year in the lookback`) TIMES ((year's `months of that year in the additional contributory period`) DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE year's `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year in the lookback`

-- Not a provision: A to F of the formula: the greater of the year's ratio of additional unadjusted
-- pensionable earnings to the (prorated) Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings and any value already determined.
-- A year whose denominator is zero has no months in the additional contributory period, so its weight in the
-- formula is zero, and the ratio is taken as zero rather than divided.
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` year MEANS
    max `the ratio` (`cp3 — the greatest of the values already determined for a month of a year` year)
    WHERE
        `the denominator` MEANS `cp3 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year of the lookback, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year
        `the ratio` MEANS
            IF `the denominator` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE (year's `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of that year`) DIVIDED BY `the denominator`

GIVEN `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the fifth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the fourth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the third year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the second year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the year of deemed disablement` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Not a provision: the formula [[(M1 x A) + (M2 x B) + ... + (M7 x G)] / R] x 0.7 of sections 51.1(1)
-- and 51.2(1). In `the year of deemed disablement` the field "months of that year in the additional
-- contributory period" holds M7, the months of the year before the month following the month of deemed
-- disablement.
`cp3 — the value determined from a disablement lookback` `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement` `the fifth year before` `the fourth year before` `the third year before` `the second year before` `the year before` `the year of deemed disablement` MEANS
    (((M1 TIMES `A`) PLUS (M2 TIMES B) PLUS (M3 TIMES C) PLUS (M4 TIMES D) PLUS (M5 TIMES E) PLUS (M6 TIMES F) PLUS (M7 TIMES G)) DIVIDED BY R) TIMES 0.7
    WHERE
        M7 MEANS `the year of deemed disablement`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        M1 MEANS min (`the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`) (12 MINUS M7)
        M2 MEANS `the fifth year before`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        M3 MEANS `the fourth year before`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        M4 MEANS `the third year before`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        M5 MEANS `the second year before`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        M6 MEANS `the year before`'s `months of that year in the additional contributory period`
        `A` MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement`
        B MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the fifth year before`
        C MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the fourth year before`
        D MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the third year before`
        E MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the second year before`
        F MEANS `cp3 — the greater of a year's ratio and the values already determined for it` `the year before`
        G MEANS
            max (min 1 `the ratio of H to I times M7 over 12`) (`cp3 — the greatest of the values already determined for a month of a year` `the year of deemed disablement`)
        `the ratio of H to I times M7 over 12` MEANS
            IF M7 EQUALS 0 OR (`the year of deemed disablement`'s `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year in the lookback`) EQUALS 0
            THEN 0
            ELSE (`the year of deemed disablement`'s `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of that year`) DIVIDED BY ((`the year of deemed disablement`'s `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year in the lookback`) TIMES (M7 DIVIDED BY 12))
        R MEANS max 1 (M1 PLUS M2 PLUS M3 PLUS M4 PLUS M5 PLUS M6 PLUS M7)


-- src:1215 | 51.1 (1) For each month that was excluded from the contributor’s contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability, a value shall be determined by the formula
-- src:1216 | [[(M1 × A) + (M2 × B) + (M3 × C) + (M4 × D) + (M5 × E) + (M6 × F) + (M7 × G)]/R] × 0.7
-- src:1217 | where
-- src:1218 | A is, in respect of the sixth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1219 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that sixth year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1220 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that sixth year;
-- src:1221 | B is, in respect of the fifth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1222 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that fifth year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1223 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that fifth year;
-- src:1224 | C is, in respect of the fourth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1225 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that fourth year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1226 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that fourth year;
-- src:1227 | D is, in respect of the third year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1228 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that third year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1229 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that third year;
-- src:1230 | E is, in respect of the second year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1231 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that second year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1232 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that second year;
-- src:1233 | F is, in respect of the year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1234 | (a) a ratio calculated by dividing the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for that prior year by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1235 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that prior year;
-- src:1236 | G is, in respect of the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the greater of
-- src:1237 | (a) the lesser of 1 and the number determined by the formula
-- src:1238 | H/[I × (M7/12)]
-- src:1239 | where
-- src:1240 | H is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year, and
-- src:1241 | I is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year, and
-- src:1242 | (b) any value that was determined in accordance with this section for a month in that year;
-- src:1243 | M1 is the lesser of
-- src:1244 | (a) the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the sixth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, and
-- src:1245 | (b) the number of months determined by the formula
-- src:1246 | 12 − M7
-- src:1247 | M2 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fifth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1248 | M3 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fourth year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1249 | M4 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the third year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1250 | M5 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the second year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1251 | M6 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled;
-- src:1252 | M7 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled that are before the month following the month in which they were deemed to have become disabled; and
-- src:1253 | R is the greater of 1 and the number of months determined by the formula
-- src:1254 | M1 + M2 + M3 + M4 + M5 + M6 + M7
@ref Act s 51.1(1) (src:1215-1254)
GIVEN `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the fifth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the fourth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the third year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the second year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
      `the year of deemed disablement` IS A `cp3 Year in a disablement lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for each month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability, a value
-- is worked out from the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the six years before
-- the year of deemed disablement and of that year, as a share of the Year's Maximum Pensionable
-- Earnings, weighted by the months of the first additional contributory period in each year, times 0.7.
-- In the lookback records, `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings` are the first additional ones.
-- out of range: sections 18 and 18.1 (piece cp1): the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings of each year of the lookback are taken as numbers.
`s 51.1(1) — the value determined for each month excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement` `the fifth year before` `the fourth year before` `the third year before` `the second year before` `the year before` `the year of deemed disablement` MEANS
    `cp3 — the value determined from a disablement lookback` `the sixth year before the year of deemed disablement` `the fifth year before` `the fourth year before` `the third year before` `the second year before` `the year before` `the year of deemed disablement`

-- src:1256 | (2) For the purposes of the descriptions of A to F in subsection (1), if the contributor’s first additional contributory period begins in the six years before the year in which they were deemed to have become disabled, the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which their first additional contributory period begins is replaced by the prorated portion determined by the formula
-- src:1257 | A × (M ÷ 12)
-- src:1258 | where
-- src:1259 | A is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor’s first additional contributory period begins; and
-- src:1260 | M is the number of months in that year that are included in the contributor’s first additional contributory period.
@ref Act s 51.1(2) (src:1256-1260)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for the descriptions of A to F of subsection (1), when the first additional contributory
-- period begins in one of the six years before the year of deemed disablement, that year's Year's
-- Maximum Pensionable Earnings is replaced by A x (M / 12). The formula of subsection (1) makes this
-- replacement itself, from the field "the additional contributory period begins in that year".
`s 51.1(2) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings replaced for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` `the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` MEANS
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` TIMES (`the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` DIVIDED BY 12)

