-- src:1309 | 51.3 For the purposes of sections 51.1 and 51.2 and despite paragraph 42(2)(b), a contributor is deemed to have become disabled at the time that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the contributor became disabled, without regard to the time when their application was made.
@ref Act s 51.3 (src:1309)
GIVEN `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the contributor became disabled` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
-- Plain gloss: for sections 51.1 and 51.2, and despite paragraph 42(2)(b), the contributor is deemed to
-- have become disabled at the time determined in the prescribed manner, whenever the application was made:
-- the fifteen-month limit of paragraph 42(2)(b) does not apply here.
`s 51.3 — the time a contributor is deemed to have become disabled for sections 51.1 and 51.2` `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the contributor became disabled` MEANS
    `the time determined in the prescribed manner to be the time when the contributor became disabled`
